`trace.mjs` uses original canonical capture-field labels and recorded file hashes/lengths. It reads the original native report, ready, bindings, independent driver JSON/log, six-state metric report, the four original start/case binaries, and only selected state5 records/loft/lift fields. Source authorities are the original ready pins mapped to immutable source-tree copies, not today's canonical sources.

The only future executable original modules are ProfileLibrary, profileFormat, dispersion and lipSheet. Installed TypeScript `transpileModule` erases each immutable source in memory using CommonJS/ESNext. A closed relative require callback/cache asserts exactly these four source names and their three original require edges; no additional module can load. Compiler version and every returned transpile diagnostic, including warnings, are recorded; errors stop the first run. A separate query-only class contains byte-extracted original sweptLoft `build`, `fronts`, `baseSlices`, `survey`, `refinements`, `at`, `planRays`, LOFT and collapseFade. These methods remain literal original source before erasure by the same compiler. Its ray callback is an explicit no-op: original ray calculations only read records and write ray outputs/diagnostics; they cannot change query sigma/tau/height/depth. The original crestRays source is pinned and its read-only prepareRecords path is asserted. This helper neither reconstructs nor validates rays. Original loftFront's profile/fade/output-count branches are reproduced narrowly to enumerate query rows; positions, masks, contact and normals are not regenerated. Original overlap count must be0 and all emitted front/sigma/tau F32 words, row count and clamp count must match, or the trace stops. Original full-precision sigma schedule is used; rounded retained sliceSigma never selects/reconstructs a query.

This is deterministic original-source reconstruction from original F32 renderer records. No direct observation of the original F64 query exists. The report distinguishes that limitation even if the complete F32 schedule and target profile Y words match. If any required source/input/word check fails, it retains the first failure and makes no approximate fallback or repair claim.

The original library's own private bracket/caseTimes/framePosition and public profileAt/frameBlend methods give normalized time, actual cases, weights, length/time scale and source frames. It evaluates and checks staged F32 arithmetic, retained Y words and lift for all57 profile points32–88 in each row. Detailed contributing frames, F64 interpolation, F32 stores, blend/scale stages, captured position words and lift are retained only for points83 and86 in each row (four detailed records total). All target core lifts and final row weights must be1. Original source-profile Y plus original config tide is checked word-for-word against retained source and mesh positions. Formation is also reproduced using original lipSheet tables. This check does not attribute a rendered fragment.

Two source-only counterfactual profiles separate size/case selection from normalized phase. The phase-first path holds row126 size and uses row127 normalized time; the size-first path holds row127 size and uses row126 normalized time. Both orders and compact X/Y deltas for all57 points are emitted; no causal percentage, physical smoothness threshold or visual quality acceptance is inferred. Counterfactuals keep drawing hold and evaluate the same original library. Their seconds are normalizedTime×the selected time unit; that recomposition is explicitly hypothetical and includes ordinary F64 arithmetic/F32 stores. This pre-execution output reduction preserves all checks and the unchanged128KiB report cap; it does not truncate inputs or post-process a failed outcome.

